# Do the Carbopol records move when only the fitter's seed changes?

Generated by `scripts/multistart_seed_scatter_carbopol.py`; every number reproduces by running it. NEXT_STEPS item 10, closing the scope gap that `solver.openfoam.check_exportable`'s docstring names: the blood seed study never covered these 15 records.

These records are independent of the blood set in every way that matters -- different material, different instrument, 54 points per curve against 16, and **the shipped values come from a different fitter** (`carbopol/fit_hb.py`, `curve_fit` on stress residuals). So seed scatter here does not move what the record ships; it moves the SIDECAR, which is why G10.3 exists.

## Pre-registered criteria

| criterion | bar | measured | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|
| G10.1 all-`measurable` records do not wander | spread <= 0.001 | 15/15 all-measurable, worst 5.409e-06 | PASS |
| G10.2 nothing the export accepts wanders | spread <= 0.001 | 15/15 accepted, worst 5.409e-06 | PASS |
| G10.3 every seed's interval contains the shipped csv value | 0 failures over 5 seeds x 3 parameters x 15 records | 0 failures | PASS |

The objective moves by at most 1.55e-11 relative across all 15 records, so nothing here is a failed search; any parameter movement is flatness.

The VERDICT SET itself is seed-dependent on 0 of 15 records, so the sidecar's verdicts are a property of the data rather than of the seed.

